Copy the hooks block from Section 5 of the blueprint into Synapse/.claude/settings.json. But start minimal — only enable SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit first:
json{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/synapse_hooks_bridge.py\"",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/synapse_hooks_bridge.py\"",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
You'll add the other hooks (Stop, TaskCompleted, TeammateIdle, etc.) one at a time after confirming each works.
Leg 5: Write the Claude Code-side bridge (stub first)
Create Synapse/.claude/hooks/synapse_hooks_bridge.py with the minimal version from Section 4 of the blueprint. Start with just the event file reader — no WebSocket commands yet. The goal is: hook fires, script reads houdini_events.jsonl, script returns context to Claude. That's it.
Test it by restarting Claude Code in the SYNAPSE directory. You should see the "Connecting SYNAPSE bridge to Houdini..." status message. If the hook errors, run claude --debug to see what went wrong.

